WEBVTT

00:02:27.276 --> 00:02:30.556
For this, participants had to muse
over statements like

00:02:30.596 --> 00:02:31.956
"Love is part of life"

00:02:31.996 --> 00:02:35.236
and "It's OK to love someone
I'm no longer with."

00:02:35.796 --> 00:02:37.916
Yeah, that changed
nothing at all for them.

00:02:37.956 --> 00:02:39.676
Overall, the researchers concluded,

00:02:39.676 --> 00:02:41.876
and I'm not using
the scientific language here,

00:02:41.916 --> 00:02:44.316
that concentrating
on the bad things about your ex

00:02:44.356 --> 00:02:46.316
can help you to feel less in love.

00:02:46.316 --> 00:02:48.556
While distracting yourself
with other subjects,

00:02:48.556 --> 00:02:49.876
as my therapist suggested,

00:02:49.876 --> 00:02:51.556
can actually make you feel better.

00:02:51.556 --> 00:02:54.876
However, the research and Dr. Tamir
would both tell you

00:02:54.916 --> 00:02:57.236
that while distraction is good
in the short term,

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:58.956
it is not a long-term solution.

00:02:58.996 --> 00:03:01.556
"Taking that time to process
and understand it